1
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:05,980
Wonderful!

2
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:07,270
Wonderful! Wonderful!

3
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,480
That one's already—

4
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,740
Ah... That hurt.

5
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:20,700
This is pain.

6
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:23,460
It makes me feel so alive.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:25,960
Damn it...

8
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:27,750
This ain't funny.

9
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:31,380
Boss did say this bitch wouldn't 
die easy, but still...

10
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:33,720
Do you dislike women such as me?

11
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:38,100
My wounds heal instantly, 
meaning I can fight forever.

12
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:42,470
Do you feel there's any point 
in fighting a woman like me?

13
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,230
Don't be dumb!

14
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:48,190
I'll just keep kickin' your ass, 
no matter how many times you heal!

15
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:51,030
How truly wonderful...

16
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,150
And that's exactly why it's so sad.

17
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,280
Huh?

18
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,950
You sense the presence 
of mabeasts, don't you?

19
00:00:57,910 --> 00:01:00,780
And it appears someone else 
is here besides your sister.

20
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,700
Isn't your concern dulling 
the force of your attacks?

21
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:08,920
Hah! Like hell it is! 
Not for Boss and his buddy!

22
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,800
No matter how many mabeasts show up,

23
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:15,380
he's just gonna laugh as 
he sends 'em all flyin'!

24
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:17,130
Nope! Nope! Nope! Nope! Can't! No way!

25
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:31,440
Did letting Garfiel work 
by himself backfire on us?

26
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:34,070
Don't sound so disheartened.

27
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:38,610
He might be out there right now, 
screaming that we're all just fine!

28
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:41,410
Subaru, are you all right?

29
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,250
I guess it's time...

30
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:53,500
to make use of my unparalleled 
knowledge of the modern world!

31
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:19,820
Bring it, you giant dog!

32
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:34,250
Taste the very spirit of science!

33
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:36,260
Dust explosion!

34
00:02:44,470 --> 00:02:45,970
Er... huh?

35
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:48,980
Wait!

36
00:02:49,350 --> 00:02:51,060
What did I tell you?!

37
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:52,860
Instead of doing weird stuff like that...

38
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,770
It's faster to do this!

39
00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:58,990
I spent all my money on this! 
It's the best oil out there!

40
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,360
Help yourself!

41
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:13,290
Spocha?!

42
00:03:25,550 --> 00:03:27,770
Did that... kill it?

43
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,850
Damn, why didn't that work?

44
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:33,270
Not enough dust? Not enough firepower?

45
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:40,030
Oh, come on!

46
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:46,530
You used too much oil!

47
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,830
Well, I couldn't very well be stingy with it!

48
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:51,080
We can't put that out! We gotta run!

49
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,460
Otto!

50
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,760
The escape route in the office 
should still be intact.

51
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:03,220
Get Rem out.

52
00:04:05,390 --> 00:04:08,560
Right. I'll take good care of her.

53
00:04:08,930 --> 00:04:10,140
Subaru?

54
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:14,350
Sorry, but I can't escape with you guys.

55
00:04:14,770 --> 00:04:16,230
We have to split up.

56
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:17,230
But why?!

57
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,730
Sorry, Petra...

58
00:04:20,070 --> 00:04:22,860
but there's one more left to save.

59
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,990
Beatrice-sama?

60
00:04:25,530 --> 00:04:29,030
Once I bring her back, be her friend, okay?

61
00:04:29,030 --> 00:04:30,660
I know you'll like her.

62
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:33,410
She's really fun to tease.

63
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:39,670
I'm counting on you guys! 
If I burn to a crisp,

64
00:04:39,670 --> 00:04:42,800
write on my gravestone that the 
cause of death was Otto's oil.

65
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,340
I have no interest in walking 
on that bed of nails.

66
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:47,850
Just come back alive, or I'll throttle you.

67
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:52,430
Subaru! Be careful!

68
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,940
<i>Face the disaster that is yet to come.</i>

69
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,770
I hate you. I hate you.

70
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,230
I hate you so much.

71
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:41,320
Since the day I met you, 
I've hated you so much,

72
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:43,530
I can't bear it.

73
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:52,910
The disaster that is yet to come?

74
00:05:53,490 --> 00:05:56,040
Does that mean this is the future?

75
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:04,210
<i>You're a hero.</i>

76
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:06,970
<i>A hero is all you can be.</i>

77
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:07,930
<i>I...</i>

78
00:06:07,930 --> 00:06:09,840
<i>Thanks for the help!</i>

79
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:11,890
<i>...you cannot even wield the 
sword without it, thief?!</i>

80
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:14,560
<i>Subaru, I know you and 
Emilia-neesama are both tired.</i>

81
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:15,980
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

82
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:19,100
<i>And yet I ended up just 
weighing you down further...</i>

83
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:21,270
<i>My precious granddaughter has grown 
into such a fine young lady, no?</i>

84
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:20,560
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

85
00:06:21,270 --> 00:06:27,240
<i>If that's the case, I should've just been 
wrapped up in that cave and left for dead!</i>

86
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:24,780
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't kill you.</i>

87
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:29,110
<i>Under no circumstances shall I be killed 
by something as nonsensical as a curse!</i>

88
00:06:27,650 --> 00:06:31,660
<i>There, you see? I win again.</i>

89
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:34,700
<i>To think someone I wanted to kill so 
badly turned out to be a kind person.</i>

90
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:40,000
<i>If I bend my knee and lose my 
sword, what is left for me?</i>

91
00:06:34,910 --> 00:06:36,660
<i>What a nightmare.</i>

92
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:43,920
<i>What's so hard about sayin' 
"I don't want to be alone"?</i>

93
00:06:42,330 --> 00:06:47,670
<i>I'm gonna kill you just like 
I promised, Natsuki Subaru!</i>

94
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,670
<i>I made the realization</i>

95
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:53,010
<i>that I have not walked alone 
all this time, that is all.</i>

96
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:58,180
<i>I suppose we must shed every last drop 
of blood in our bodies to atone.</i>

97
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,890
<i>You can just stand there running in place!</i>

98
00:06:56,890 --> 00:07:01,770
<i>Magic, dragons, whatever stands 
in my way, I'll destroy it!</i>

99
00:06:58,230 --> 00:07:00,730
<i>Why won't the soul take hold?!</i>

100
00:07:07,150 --> 00:07:11,490
<i>I believe praying to ask 
for a favor is arrogant.</i>

101
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,120
<i>Prayer should be for seeking forgiveness.</i>

102
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,770
Is this...

103
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:50,030
Echidna?

104
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:57,490
You will regret reaching out so readily

105
00:07:57,490 --> 00:07:59,700
for a feast offered by a witch.

106
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:08,800
Good girl. Not turning 
around is the right choice.

107
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:10,710
Wh-Who are you?

108
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,930
I'm, um... you know...

109
00:08:12,930 --> 00:08:16,550
a witch so terrifying, 
it'll make your hair stand on end!

110
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:22,140
Where's Echidna?

111
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:26,980
Well, she said she doesn't want to see you.

112
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:29,780
She must have had a terrible 
time in the trial.

113
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:31,740
I guess so.

114
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:36,870
I hurt her really badly at the end of it.

115
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:41,830
How did the third trial look to you?

116
00:08:42,450 --> 00:08:45,330
I saw lots of very sad worlds.

117
00:08:46,330 --> 00:08:48,670
Was that really the future?

118
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:51,420
It was a possible one.

119
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:55,130
Of course, showing you 
only unpleasant futures

120
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:57,930
was undoubtedly her way of bullying you.

121
00:08:59,390 --> 00:09:03,810
Yeah. Echidna is definitely a mean girl.

122
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:06,650
You're content with just calling that "mean"?

123
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:11,280
How can you look so relaxed?

124
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,110
Huh?

125
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:13,690
Well, it's just weird.

126
00:09:13,690 --> 00:09:17,530
You saw all those terrible futures, and yet...

127
00:09:17,530 --> 00:09:20,030
But it's not guaranteed, right?

128
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:22,750
A future like that is possible,

129
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:25,660
but there's a chance it won't be like that.

130
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,880
As long as I know that, it's fine.

131
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:30,670
I can always fight it.

132
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:35,630
You don't think you'll break right away?

133
00:09:36,050 --> 00:09:38,300
If I was alone, maybe.

134
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:42,100
But they won't let me be alone.

135
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,390
You're pretty strong.

136
00:09:44,770 --> 00:09:47,980
That part of you is nothing like your mother.

137
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:51,020
Huh?! Are you saying you know my—

138
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:54,590
Yes, I know her well,
but I can't tell you more.

139
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,280
I promised I wouldn't.

140
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:01,240
I understand.

141
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:04,290
I won't ask you anything, then.

142
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:05,790
You're sure?

143
00:10:06,410 --> 00:10:08,170
I know what it's like when 
you can't say something,

144
00:10:08,170 --> 00:10:09,920
rather than just not wanting to.

145
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:11,250
Besides...

146
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:16,720
My mother is Mother Fortuna.

147
00:10:20,470 --> 00:10:21,970
I see.

148
00:10:24,430 --> 00:10:28,350
I guess her evil plots 
do good things sometimes.

149
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:31,520
Are you... crying?

150
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:33,020
I'm not crying!

151
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,110
I don't cry. I don't have 
the right to cry now.

152
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:39,200
Nobody needs to have the right to—

153
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:47,660
What did I tell you? Not turning 
around was the right choice.

154
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:52,080
You're a bad girl.

155
00:10:58,050 --> 00:11:01,180
Go straight ahead, 
and the trial will be over.

156
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:03,970
The barrier will be opened.

157
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:12,860
Hey, witch...

158
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:16,440
If you see Echidna, could you 
tell her something for me?

159
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:17,690
What?

160
00:11:18,610 --> 00:11:21,700
Next time we meet, let's have a tea party.

161
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:25,700
With you and the other witches, if possible.

162
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:30,710
Sure, I'll tell her.

163
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:34,420
If she doesn't want to come, I'll drag
 her there by the scruff of her neck!

164
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,520
It's open...

165
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:24,840
Who is this?

166
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:28,890
This should be Echidna's grave...

167
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:39,570
Wow... This is the spell 
generating the barrier?

168
00:12:39,570 --> 00:12:43,780
It's so incredible, I have 
no idea what it's doing.

169
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:52,750
I think... right here.

170
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,570
Yeah. It just ended.

171
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:34,870
I need to tell all the people 
who are waiting for me.

172
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:41,800
Huh?!

173
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:58,440
What did I tell ya?

174
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:02,020
Mabeasts are a piece o' cake for the boss!

175
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:04,900
Don't you think you might 
be overestimating him?

176
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:16,500
Come on, Rock Piggie! Get up already!

177
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:19,330
Maylie, I was hoping 
you'd stay out of my way.

178
00:14:19,330 --> 00:14:20,080
Elsa?!

179
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:24,800
Ugh! I had to go through so much 
work because you rushed things!

180
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,590
Show a little remorse, would you?!

181
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:27,880
Garf!

182
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,260
This is where you were?

183
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:31,720
Big Sis?! Why the hell are you still here?!

184
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,600
Where's Boss and the kid?!

185
00:14:32,890 --> 00:14:35,470
I have completed the mission entrusted to me.

186
00:14:35,470 --> 00:14:38,810
You know why I remain here, do you not?

187
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:45,940
You sisters sure are givin' us hell!

188
00:14:46,990 --> 00:14:47,990
Sisters?

189
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:50,990
Yes, we are sisters.

190
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:56,450
So it seems that, oddly enough, 
both of our sibling duos are complete.

191
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:04,090
Can I assume this is a good 
time for a fresh start?

192
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,390
Garf, do not worry about my—

193
00:15:15,390 --> 00:15:16,060
Hah!

194
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:20,640
They say the Master Swordsman Reid laughed 
as he drew his sword against a dragon!

195
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:23,980
That's an idiom used to 
describe someone who's crazy.

196
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:25,610
Yep, I know!

197
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,910
That's my divine protection of earth spirits.

198
00:15:36,910 --> 00:15:39,080
So long as my feet are on the ground,

199
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:42,210
everything I can see is 
within my strike range!

200
00:15:42,790 --> 00:15:45,880
Maylie, don't take a single step forward.

201
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:49,720
Big Sis, stay behind me and watch.

202
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,200
Garf! I will handle this one!

203
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,250
Rock Piggie!

204
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:35,260
Get crushed flat!

205
00:17:07,790 --> 00:17:09,250
N-No...

206
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:10,880
No!

207
00:17:11,550 --> 00:17:12,510
Elsa!

208
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:14,130
Do something!

209
00:17:14,130 --> 00:17:16,930
What a slave-driver you are.

210
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:27,310
While your body becomes injured all over,

211
00:17:27,310 --> 00:17:29,480
my wounds continue to heal themselves.

212
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:32,650
Are you starting to find it unfair?

213
00:17:32,990 --> 00:17:34,320
Huh?

214
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,530
I ain't broken yet.

215
00:17:36,530 --> 00:17:39,450
If I just keep killin' ya 
until you die, you'll die.

216
00:17:39,910 --> 00:17:41,990
Right, vampire?!

217
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:44,200
You know?

218
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:47,290
I always liked readin' books.

219
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,540
One of the witches was a 
vampire a long time ago.

220
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:53,840
That witch is dead, so I can kill you, too.

221
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:57,840
If you swear you'll never do bad shit again,

222
00:17:58,220 --> 00:18:00,300
I might just let ya off the hook.

223
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:03,850
You really are absolutely precious.

224
00:18:06,390 --> 00:18:09,400
Gusteco, the land to the 
north where I was born,

225
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,360
was a very, very cold place.

226
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,070
I was abandoned as a child.

227
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:17,860
I hurt people and stole 
from them day after day.

228
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:21,990
I had no time to think about things 
like living or being happy.

229
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:25,450
One day, during a blizzard, 
I was stealing from a shop,

230
00:18:25,450 --> 00:18:27,460
and its owner captured me.

231
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:29,290
Shut up! No one asked!

232
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:33,250
Since I was a girl, he took off both 
my clothes and my underclothes...

233
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:37,050
But I just happened to find a shard of glass.

234
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:39,300
I didn't give it any thought.

235
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:42,140
I just drove it into his belly.

236
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:47,810
At that moment, even as I felt like 
I might freeze in that blizzard,

237
00:18:48,190 --> 00:18:49,770
I had a thought...

238
00:18:52,610 --> 00:18:57,240
Blood and innards are so very warm.

239
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:02,370
If there is happiness in this world,

240
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:05,290
it is the warmth that 
makes one forget the cold.

241
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,290
It was the first happiness I ever found.

242
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:10,290
You can't understand that, can you?

243
00:19:10,290 --> 00:19:13,790
If ya know that, why the hell 
did ya blather on about it?

244
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,800
Why, indeed...

245
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:20,180
It must be because you're so very endearing.

246
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:22,850
Sorry, but there's already a girl I like.

247
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:25,930
I ain't got time for some psycho bitch!

248
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:27,470
How cold.

249
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:29,270
But that's all right.

250
00:19:29,890 --> 00:19:34,150
It's only your insides 
that I have business with.

251
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:37,480
I will kill you, Elsa Granhiert.

252
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:42,820
My love for you will begin after 
I kill you, Garfiel Tinzel.

253
00:20:10,390 --> 00:20:12,600
Elsa!

254
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,720
What a thrill.

255
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:34,640
Love Me Down to My Blood and Guts

256
00:21:39,650 --> 00:21:41,070
You all right?

257
00:21:41,070 --> 00:21:43,650
Being too reckless is bad for you, y'know.

258
00:21:43,650 --> 00:21:45,360
No need for concern.

259
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:49,120
Thanks to you, Great Spirit, 
at least I'm able to fight.

260
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:52,040
I was correct to bring you outside.

261
00:21:52,620 --> 00:22:00,340
I can't have that place—specifically, 
that magic crystal—destroyed.

262
00:22:00,710 --> 00:22:04,670
Of course, you should still 
be able to achieve your goal.

263
00:22:04,670 --> 00:22:06,720
Will you not attempt to do so?

264
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:09,220
You mean I should ask the 
great spirit to stall you,

265
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:11,180
and use that opening?

266
00:22:13,020 --> 00:22:14,270
You jest.

267
00:22:14,810 --> 00:22:19,900
Even if I do that, my wish 
will never be fulfilled.

268
00:22:21,610 --> 00:22:25,320
That said, things will only 
get worse if we continue.

269
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:29,370
You did strike terror in me, 
but even a great spirit is not perfect.

270
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:32,830
I have to commend your meticulousness.

271
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:34,830
When did you put the spell on Lia?

272
00:22:36,830 --> 00:22:39,080
Before heading for the Sanctuary.

273
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:42,630
Doctoring the contract 
between you and Emilia-sama

274
00:22:42,630 --> 00:22:46,050
while she was depressed after a 
fight with Subaru-kun was simple.

275
00:22:46,590 --> 00:22:49,930
You wanted Lia to stay discouraged?

276
00:22:49,930 --> 00:22:51,010
Yes.

277
00:22:51,010 --> 00:22:55,390
Restricting Subaru-kun's actions 
took more effort than anything else.

278
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:59,310
He is the last key to the 
unlocking of my dearest wish.

279
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:06,530
Unlike you, I am not merely testing him to 
see if he is worthy of my dear daughter.

280
00:23:06,530 --> 00:23:09,530
Don't get cocky, witch's disciple.

281
00:23:10,990 --> 00:23:16,040
Am I correct in guessing that you now 
remember what happened before your contract?

282
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:18,460
There are plenty of guesses you could make.

283
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:18,870
But...

284
00:23:19,750 --> 00:23:23,340
I was remembering a man 
who spoke a lot like you.

285
00:23:24,210 --> 00:23:27,670
Is it so I'd remember that wound,
 or perhaps a warning?

286
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:30,590
Either way, it's just backward-facing.

287
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,890
Backward-facing, indeed...

288
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:39,940
Yes, of course. I am forever 
looking back upon the past.

289
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:44,230
For me, all the wonderful things 
that ever happened were in the past.

290
00:23:44,650 --> 00:23:49,190
All that exists now is a phony 
standing atop a pile of corpses.

291
00:23:50,530 --> 00:23:53,280
I'm not going to find 
fault with what you are.

292
00:23:53,990 --> 00:23:54,740
But...

293
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:56,450
What?

294
00:23:56,660 --> 00:23:59,410
You're going to make Betty sad, Roswaal.

295
00:24:00,910 --> 00:24:03,080
Ul Goa!

296
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:06,170
What a childish way to react 
just because I hit the bull's-eye!

297
00:24:09,130 --> 00:24:10,130
El Fu—

298
00:24:10,130 --> 00:24:10,720
Too late.

299
00:24:11,430 --> 00:24:12,380
Get back!

300
00:24:15,890 --> 00:24:18,720
If you don't get up now, the next 
one'll hit you, and you'll lose.

301
00:24:19,180 --> 00:24:21,190
You make it sound so simple...

302
00:24:21,890 --> 00:24:24,730
I could not be more disappointed, Ram.

303
00:24:28,570 --> 00:24:30,150
I wanted your wish to come true.

304
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:35,530
I wanted you to exact justice for 
your brethren and find happiness.

305
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,660
Ram?

306
00:24:42,290 --> 00:24:44,080
After repeating it so many times,

307
00:24:44,710 --> 00:24:46,380
after touching upon it so many times,

308
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:49,670
you still haven't realized 
my true intentions.

309
00:24:50,960 --> 00:24:52,880
I only wish I was just a demon

310
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:57,430
burning with hatred in her 
wish to avenge her brethren.

311
00:24:58,180 --> 00:25:00,430
If I were only out for revenge,

312
00:25:01,270 --> 00:25:04,020
my heart would not hurt so.

313
00:25:05,770 --> 00:25:06,730
But...

314
00:25:09,110 --> 00:25:09,940
Roswaal-sama,

315
00:25:11,490 --> 00:25:12,900
I...

316
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:17,570
love you.

317
00:25:22,410 --> 00:25:23,870
Is something wrong?

318
00:25:24,670 --> 00:25:26,670
Wrong?

319
00:25:26,670 --> 00:25:29,630
Are you making fun of me? After all this?

320
00:25:29,630 --> 00:25:31,670
I only said what I truly feel.

321
00:25:31,670 --> 00:25:34,220
I know that can't be true!

322
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:37,090
You love me? How dare you say that?!

323
00:25:37,090 --> 00:25:38,260
I am the one you hate!

324
00:25:38,260 --> 00:25:41,810
I am the man who caused the 
destruction of your homeland!

325
00:25:41,810 --> 00:25:45,020
I know you hated me so much 
that you wanted to kill me!

326
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:48,860
That was true at first, but not now.

327
00:25:49,190 --> 00:25:51,320
What's true now is...

328
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:53,570
I love you.

329
00:25:54,990 --> 00:25:58,820
Who would believe in such a cheap emotion?!

330
00:25:58,820 --> 00:26:00,160
What of your revenge?

331
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:03,200
Did you not swear on the souls 
of your brethren to achieve it?!

332
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:06,080
I do feel as if I've wronged my brethren.

333
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:09,340
But I cannot help that I love you.

334
00:26:09,340 --> 00:26:13,090
I will prioritize my own feelings 
over those of the dead.

335
00:26:13,710 --> 00:26:14,970
Great Spirit!

336
00:26:14,970 --> 00:26:16,050
You got it!

337
00:26:16,050 --> 00:26:20,350
Next to my beloved daughter, it's girls 
in love that I'll always side with!

338
00:26:31,230 --> 00:26:32,400
Petty tricks!

339
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:40,240
Where are you looking?

340
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:44,750
It can't be...

341
00:26:53,250 --> 00:26:57,090
Surprise! I just got bigger, that's all!

342
00:27:27,290 --> 00:27:28,660
Wh-What...

343
00:27:38,470 --> 00:27:39,550
That's—

344
00:27:40,510 --> 00:27:42,680
As far as I'm concerned,

345
00:27:42,680 --> 00:27:45,960
this is the root of all evil.

346
00:28:18,590 --> 00:28:20,970
Now, at last...

